WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.442
This course uses vw as a prefix for standard views and mv for materialized views.

00:00:06.442 --> 00:00:09.792
PostgreSQL does not require that naming convention.

00:00:09.792 --> 00:00:11.602
The goal is readability and discoverability.

00:00:11.602 --> 00:00:18.482
Whatever convention a team chooses, use it consistently and document the intended grain and meaning of

00:00:18.482 --> 00:00:18.782
important shared objects.

00:00:18.782 --> 00:00:24.312
Connect this idea to a governance project limiting which columns different users can access.

00:00:24.312 --> 00:00:29.472
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:29.472 --> 00:00:36.747
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:36.747 --> 00:00:41.757
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:41.757 --> 00:00:47.280
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
